# External SSH for heavy work

Default to the external build host for anything disk- or CPU-heavy. Local machine stays for editing, small tests, and git.

## Host

```bash
ssh -p 22488 gosh@94.156.178.14   # hostname: n14
```

- Home: `/home/gosh` (98G root FS)
- Large scratch: `/mnt/data/gosh/` (3.3T data volume)
- Passwordless `sudo` available
- No secrets or irreplaceable data — wipe scratch dirs freely after sessions

## Use remote for

- `cargo build --release` on acki-nacki, prover, circuits, tvm-sdk
- Docker 5-node AN cluster (`acki-nacki/nock/docker-compose`)
- Prover/verifier daemons, long Halo2 proving runs
- Cached `params/` keys, `target/release`, proof artefacts
- E2E runbook steps (Circuit 4 withdrawal, verifyBlock bundles)

## Keep local

- Source edits and git commits
- Foundry `forge test` (fast contract tests)
- Small unit tests that finish in seconds

## Remote workspace layout

```bash
/mnt/data/gosh/acki-nacki/        # AN node cluster (poseidon_dex); docker compose via make run
/mnt/data/gosh/sergey-bridge/     # prover scratch root
  acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/
  acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-circuits/
  acki-nacki-bridge/
  params/
  proofs/
  logs/
```

Clone or `rsync` only what the task needs. Do not touch other users' dirs under `/mnt/data/gosh/{nikita,alina,misha,...}`.

## Sync pattern

```bash
# one-shot: tunnel + sync + bk_set + wipe stale proofs + start daemons
acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/scripts/run_n14_prover_stack.sh

# manual sync
rsync -avz --exclude target --exclude params -e "ssh -p 22488" \
  /home/sergey/Pruvendo/gosh/acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/ \
  gosh@94.156.178.14:/mnt/data/gosh/sergey-bridge/acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/

# BK set must match the running docker cluster (after every fresh compose up)
acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/scripts/extract_bk_set_from_docker.sh

# pull proofs/logs back
rsync -avz -e "ssh -p 22488" \
  gosh@94.156.178.14:/mnt/data/gosh/sergey-bridge/acki-nacki-to-eth-bridge-halo2-prover/proofs/ \
  ./proofs/
```

**Gotchas (2026-06-07):**
- Wipe `proofs/proof_*.json` + `proofs/result_*.json` before a clean run — verifier skips seqnos it already processed.
- Rebuild binaries **on n14** (`cargo build --release`); rsync'd `target/release/*` from local may fail with `GLIBC_2.38 not found`.
- `make run` on n14 needs `source ~/.cargo/env` and `CMD_PREFIX=sudo` (root-owned `docker/ton-live/web/storage/node*`).
- **Full E2E on n14**: cluster GraphQL is local on n14 — run prover with `BRIDGE_GQL_ENDPOINT=http://localhost/graphql` (no reverse tunnel). Tunnel (`127.0.0.1:18080`) only when the cluster runs locally and prover on n14.

## Cleanup after sessions

```bash
ssh -p 22488 gosh@94.156.178.14 'sudo rm -rf /mnt/data/gosh/sergey-bridge/target /mnt/data/gosh/sergey-bridge/*/target'
docker compose down -v   # in cluster dir; sudo rm if root-owned volumes remain
docker volume prune -f && docker builder prune -af
```

## SSH in commands

Use `ssh -o BatchMode=yes -p 22488 gosh@94.156.178.14 '...'` for non-interactive runs. Long jobs: `nohup` or `tmux` on remote.
